y. Opening the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01G39ULn5rpKwomqYW3ZcMq9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18). Release history: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy; v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Actions taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt to v2.3.0 completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up needed: investigate the v2.3.1 regression and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it has been fixed and validated."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll check whether it was created before retrying, so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018hnzicX4K7fGQsmDcrEJ1Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, which left the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried once and it completed in all regions. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The first incident request timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else; it showed the incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the actions above.\n\nFollow-up needed: someone should investigate the v2.3.1 regression and the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and validated.", "type": "text"}]}]}